01:10:27.640 --> 01:10:29.130
And this is a--

01:10:29.130 --> 01:10:31.170
people have spent a
lot of time trying

01:10:31.170 --> 01:10:32.340
to deal with that question.

01:10:35.090 --> 01:10:36.890
And here is the--

01:10:44.420 --> 01:10:45.860
so how you stack--

01:10:45.860 --> 01:11:01.855
thermostat the ensemble--
thermostatted ensembles.

01:11:11.040 --> 01:11:18.170
So to do this, you actually also
have to get used to the fact

01:11:18.170 --> 01:11:21.810
that normally you
do F equals ma.

01:11:21.810 --> 01:11:23.620
That's the equation of motion.

01:11:23.620 --> 01:11:28.140
But there are many different
ways to write the F equals ma.

01:11:28.140 --> 01:11:31.050
And there are
[INAUDIBLE] equation

01:11:31.050 --> 01:11:34.390
of motion, Hamiltonian
equation of motion.

01:11:34.390 --> 01:11:36.960
They are all equivalent.

01:11:36.960 --> 01:11:38.880
Not [INAUDIBLE],,
Lagrangian equation

01:11:38.880 --> 01:11:41.430
of motion and Hamiltonian.

01:11:41.430 --> 01:11:51.210
So for example, when you do a
Lagrangian equation of motion.

01:11:55.630 --> 01:12:05.030
And what you use is r, r dot.

01:12:05.030 --> 01:12:14.680
You use this the velocity and
space, say, as your variable.

01:12:14.680 --> 01:12:20.020
And you construct the
Lagrangian of the system, which

01:12:20.020 --> 01:12:22.210
