01:12:33.920 --> 01:12:38.460
So it's kinetic energy
minus potential energy.

01:12:38.460 --> 01:12:40.950
Maybe you learn
this in dynamics.

01:12:40.950 --> 01:12:45.750
And so, the Hamiltonian
principle-- so what's

01:12:45.750 --> 01:12:48.330
the Lagrangian
equation of motion?

01:12:48.330 --> 01:12:50.850
Is there is this
Hamiltonian principle,

01:12:50.850 --> 01:12:54.450
say when your system
go from point one

01:12:54.450 --> 01:12:59.420
to point two, the Lagrangian--

01:12:59.420 --> 01:13:03.770
so the integral
here, integral-- this

01:13:03.770 --> 01:13:08.750
is actually integral from
1 to 2 of the Lagrangian,

01:13:08.750 --> 01:13:12.740
and tr, r dot.

01:13:12.740 --> 01:13:15.090
And they integrate over time.

01:13:15.090 --> 01:13:17.630
And this should be extreme.

01:13:17.630 --> 01:13:19.600
It's a maximum or minimum.

01:13:19.600 --> 01:13:21.100
And in fact, I don't
know whether it

01:13:21.100 --> 01:13:22.820
