01:13:29.810 --> 01:13:35.880
You actually get the equation
of motion for the Lagrangian.

01:13:35.880 --> 01:13:39.120
So you do your--

01:13:39.120 --> 01:13:42.280
here you do the
equation of motion.

01:13:42.280 --> 01:13:45.300
Then you will get,
this is the extrema.

01:13:45.300 --> 01:13:51.550
You'll get a dL, dr.

01:13:51.550 --> 01:13:53.110
Here, I have--

01:13:53.110 --> 01:13:57.610
I'm writing in each
component the velocity.

01:13:57.610 --> 01:14:03.340
And dL dr itself equals 0.

01:14:03.340 --> 01:14:08.140
So this is the actually F
equal ma under the Lagrangian.

01:14:11.970 --> 01:14:16.990
The Lagrangian is useful.

01:14:16.990 --> 01:14:20.210
But it has one defect.

01:14:20.210 --> 01:14:23.580
It's not symmetric.

01:14:23.580 --> 01:14:25.410
It lacks symmetry.

01:14:25.410 --> 01:14:29.600
And so, if you-- rather
than use r and r dot,

01:14:29.600 --> 01:14:34.490
if you use r and p, this will
come back to the face space.

01:14:34.490 --> 01:14:39.320
If you use the position and
momentum, and you actually

01:14:39.320 --> 01:14:43.580
can do a transformation into the
Hamiltonian equation of motion.

01:14:52.440 --> 01:14:56.000
So you can write,
rather than using

01:14:56.000 --> 01:15:01.010
r, if you do your new
variable p momentum,

01:15:01.010 --> 01:15:09.440
if you define equals the
Lagrangian derivative, that's

01:15:09.440 --> 01:15:10.160
a momentum.

01:15:10.160 --> 01:15:12.860
And you can go write a
Cartesian coordinate,

01:15:12.860 --> 01:15:16.100
and you'll find this all
come back to F equal ma.

01:15:16.100 --> 01:15:17.690
Everything makes sense.

01:15:17.690 --> 01:15:24.560
And then you can construct
your Hamiltonian trp.

01:15:24.560 --> 01:15:30.470
So now, my variable in
Lagrangian is r and r dot.

01:15:30.470 --> 01:15:34.240
In Hamiltonian is r and p.

01:15:34.240 --> 01:15:48.430
So this is sigma
dL dri, ri minus L.

01:15:48.430 --> 01:15:52.820
And you can say, in
this simple, say,

01:15:52.820 --> 01:15:58.150
case for kinetic plus
potential is essentially

01:15:58.150 --> 01:16:00.490
if you're using Cartesian
coordinate, and you will say,

01:16:00.490 --> 01:16:02.930
